module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.heal_converge_overruns_the_90_minute_cap_on_a_contended_runner_when_the_rebuilt_seed_round_pages

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data heal_converge_overruns_the_90_minute_cap_on_a_contended_runner_when_the_rebuilt_seed_round_pages: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "heal_converge_overruns_the_90_minute_cap_on_a_contended_runner_when_the_rebuilt_seed_round_pages" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "Bind the memory envelope named by gunbc.host.memory_envelope (memory.high throttles early, memory.max refuses late, MemorySwapMax 0 refuses an overrun rather than paging it) around the heal converge seed builds, and read every fleet runner unit against its declared runner_slot_desired before a heal run is admitted, so the memory-heaviest rebuilt-seed round is either bounded (refused fast) or placed on a fast, less-contended unit. Sufficient for: that round cannot silently consume the whole 90-minute budget by paging on a loaded host. This is a fleet-capacity and memory-envelope decision, not a compiler change, and it does not touch the 90-minute cap itself, which is the operator's to set." } },

  receipts: [
    "**heal converge overruns the 90-minute cap when the rebuilt-seed round pages on a contended runner** (an environmental timeout read as a compiler defect). The heal-generated-artifacts step 'Converge the stage0 mirrors to the seed's own fixed point' runs `claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror` and is capped at 90 minutes; a healthy run finishes the converge step in ~33-36 minutes (job ~42-45). When it blows the cap the cheap read is 'the regen hung' or 'this PR's mirrors are expensive'. Neither is true; the work is identical, only the wall-clock per phase moves, because the job runs on the shared self-hosted pool (machines srv3, srv4) and the convergence's memory-heaviest phase is unbounded.",

    "IT IS NOT A HANG. The convergence round count is bounded by `v1_compiler.required_regen_host::regen_convergence_generation_bound`, so there is no unbounded loop to hang in. The '55 minutes of silence' that made run 41240308313 (PR #15527, head 2f3cd05e, runner srv3-12-1793479415-4005434) look frozen at `round.built_seed_regen` was the CHILD's stderr being discarded: `run_built_seed_regen` used to spawn `spawn_rebuilt_seed_regen_child` on `Command::output()`, which buffers and drops the child's per-phase trace, so a ~53-minute phase sat silent in the job log while the child worked. That blind spot is already repaired on main by gunb-ai/gunbc#15594 (commit f64821c7), which forwards the child with `RebuiltSeedChildOutput::ForwardToJobLog`; the killed builds predate it (heads 2f3cd05e dated 2026-10-31, ce61ceb7 dated 2026-10-29; the fix merged 2026-11-01). A silent `built_seed_regen` on a post-#15594 head would be a different, real finding.",

    "IT IS NOT A COST REGRESSION ON INPUTS. The regen plan is byte-identical across the killed and the good runs -- `planned=176 executed=176 adjudicated=176` on all four specimens below, no mirror or round added. The extra time is not more work; it is the same cargo/rustc-bound phases at 2-4x wall-clock on a loaded host.",

    "THE MECHANISM IS CONTENTION, AND IT TRACKS THE RUNNER UNIT, NOT THE CODE. Two killed runs, two signatures, both environmental: (a) run 40938516623 (PR #15388 head ce61ceb7, runner srv4-05-1793363381-2383450) was UNIFORMLY slow -- `round.seed_build` 17 min and 12 min, `compile.emit` 11 min, `compile.reconcile` 3 min, required-regen `elapsed_ms` 1342703 -- against healthy values of 4-5 min / 4-5 min / ~70 s / ~590000-650000; every phase moved together, which is a loaded host, then it was cancelled mid post-regen typecheck. (b) run 41240308313 (head 2f3cd05e, runner srv3-12-1793479415-4005434) ran its first ~30 minutes at NORMAL speed (`round.seed_build` 4 min, `compile.emit` 5 min, required-regen `elapsed_ms` 662259) and then spent the entire remainder inside `round.built_seed_regen` -- the seed rebuild plus a full second `--required-regen` pass in the child, the most memory-hungry phase -- which took >55 min on srv3 and was killed at the cap. Same code, same plan, wildly different durations, split by which runner unit the job landed on.",

    "A SECOND, INPUT-TRIGGERED AMPLIFIER PUSHES THE TIPPING POINT CLOSER. Whether the extra round runs at all is decided by `first_generation_equal` = `sync.matches && hand.unverifiable.is_empty()` in `v1_compiler.required_regen_host::run_regen_round_cost`: when the first regenerated generation is not yet the fixed point (`first_generation_equal = false`), the step pays `round.rebuild_from_installed` + `round.install` + `round.built_seed_regen` -- a whole extra `--required-regen` in the child, ~11-15 min at healthy speed -- on top of the ~40-minute baseline. The two good runs had `first_generation_equal = true` and skipped it; run 2f3cd05e had `false` and paid it. So a pull request whose own seed is not immediately a fixed point has only ~35-40 minutes of headroom before the cap, and a 2x host slowdown -- which the srv3/srv4 pool delivers under load -- tips it over.",

    "THE MEMORY ENVELOPE IS NOT ON THIS STEP. The converge step emits `memory-cgroup-bind: not requested`, i.e. `v1_compiler.memory_governor::CgroupBindDecision::NotRequested`, so the seed builds run with no `memory.max`/`memory.high` bound. DESIGN section on fabric/compute records that the isolation authority for the shared self-hosted pool is the SLOT plus `gunbc.host.memory_envelope` (memory.high throttles early, memory.max refuses late, MemorySwapMax 0 refuses an overrun rather than paging it), and that live runner units DRIFT from that declared shape -- a `MemorySwapMax` of 32 GiB where the slot declares 0, read on the fleet 2026-10-21, the class at `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `the_live_runner_unit_memory_shape_drifts_from_the_declared_slot`. Unbound and with swap allowed, the memory-heaviest round does not get refused fast -- it pages, and paging is what turns a ~11-minute phase into a ~55-minute one.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT A FAILING CHANGE: the killed heads (2f3cd05e on PR #15527, ce61ceb7 on PR #15388) carry no defect that would slow their own regeneration; a re-run of the same head on an unloaded unit (srv4-09, srv4-10 are where the good runs landed) completes the converge step in ~33-36 minutes. Treating a cap overrun as a defect in the pull request invites the DESIGN section 5 concealment -- weakening the change, or reaching to raise the cap, to hide a host-side deficit.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a heal converge round is bounded (refused fast) or fast is a decidable placement-and-envelope fact of the fleet, not an undecidable property of the input; with the envelope enforced and units read against `runner_slot_desired`, no phase can silently page its way past a cap.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: bind the memory envelope around the heal converge seed builds and schedule the rebuilt-seed round on a heal-reserved or measured-fast unit, and gate heal admission on a live read of each runner unit against its declared `gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired` (refusing a unit whose `MemorySwapMax` has drifted from the declared 0). Until that trigger runs, heal convergence wall-clock rests on a declared authority that DESIGN already says is not fully installed.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a heal-generated-artifacts cancel at the 90-minute cap on a head whose regen plan size (planned/executed/adjudicated) matches a known-green run's, and whose job log shows normal-speed early phases but a `round.built_seed_regen` (or a uniformly slow `round.seed_build` / `compile.emit`) -- read the runner name and `elapsed_ms` before reading the diff.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.host.memory_envelope", decl_name: "memory_envelope_enforcement", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.the_live_runner_unit_memory_shape_drifts_from_the_declared_slot", decl_name: "the_live_runner_unit_memory_shape_drifts_from_the_declared_slot", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.heal_workflow", decl_name: "heal_workflow_required_bins", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
